      <div class="hcm-or-hd"><span class="hcm-or-eyebrow">Quick Verdict</span><h2>Quick Verdict: Are Infinity Massage Chairs Worth It?</h2></div>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Is Infinity worth it?</strong> For the right buyer, yes — especially when the model matches your body fit, intensity preference, and the feature set you actually plan to use. Infinity appeals strongest to shoppers who want a wide range of model tiers, from value-oriented 4D options like Riage 4D to flagship Circadian DualFlex 4D and luxury Syner-D models.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">When Infinity is a strong fit:</strong> You want 4D roller feel, deep body scanning, gravity positions, and lower-body comfort (foot rollers, calf massage). You plan to test in a showroom before deciding. You value brand options across multiple feature tiers and price points.</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--ink)">When to consider alternatives:</strong> You want a single fixed feature set across the lineup. You prefer a different brand language for controls. You haven't narrowed down massage intensity preference yet — in that case, compare Infinity in person against Osaki, Kyota, or Ogawa before deciding.</p>
